## How to work
- Do one story at a time. Keep changes small and reversible.
- Put new code in the module that owns that responsibility. If none fits,
  stop and ask; don't invent a new dependency direction.
- Write tests for every behaviour you add or change.

## Definition of done
Your work is done only when this command exits 0:

    make check

If it fails, read the output, fix the cause (not the gate), and run it again.
Never edit the gate configuration (thresholds, `fence.toml`) to make it pass.
That's a design decision for a human.
